{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 133, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed restores trainability, whereas replacing an existing conv path gains far less."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is none, node 2's computation is unused, so adding a conv there newly connects a whole branch to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 already absent, deleting edge 0 leaves nodes 1 and 2 empty, so the cell collapses to the edge-3 path alone."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling a missing node1-to-output edge adds a new computational path, which helps more than replacing an existing skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the residual skip harms optimization of the deep stacked network much more than removing a conv on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is also none, removing edge 4 leaves only the direct edge-3 path to the output, wiping out all cell computation."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none with conv3x3 adds depth and a new route, while replacing conv1x1, skip or pool is only a marginal change."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, node 2 does not reach the output, so changing edge 2 has essentially no effect."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 absent, removing edge 1 leaves node 2 with no inputs, killing the edge-5 path entirely."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on an empty edge 3 adds capacity, whereas swapping it in for the residual skip removes the beneficial shortcut."}], "tok": 32177, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_co